```javascript
function cleanAndExport() {
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const raw = ss.getSheetByName('Raw');
  if (!raw) throw new Error('Sheet "Raw" not found.');

  const lastRow = raw.getLastRow();
  if (lastRow < 2) return;

  // Columns: A=1 Timestamp, B=2 Name, C=3 Email, D=4 JoinedBefore, E=5 Phone,
  // F=6 PreferredPark, G=7 YN, H=8 Phone, I=9 TS, J=10 Park,
  // K=11 emailKey, L=12 nameKey, M=13 DUP-email, N=14 DUP-name-time,
  // O=15 Superseded, P=16 Review
  const numRows = lastRow - 1;
  const data = raw.getRange(2, 1, numRows, 16).getValues();

  // --- Step 1: SUPERSEDED per email (keep most recent timestamp in col I) ---
  const latestByEmail = {}; // emailKey -> { ts, rowIdx }
  data.forEach((row, i) => {
    const emailKey = String(row[10] || '').trim(); // col K
    const ts = row[8];                             // col I
    if (!emailKey || !(ts instanceof Date) && typeof ts !== 'number') return;
    const tsVal = ts instanceof Date ? ts.getTime() : Number(ts);
    if (isNaN(tsVal)) return;
    if (!latestByEmail[emailKey] || tsVal > latestByEmail[emailKey].ts) {
      latestByEmail[emailKey] = { ts: tsVal, rowIdx: i };
    }
  });

  data.forEach((row, i) => {
    const emailKey = String(row[10] || '').trim();
    if (!emailKey) { row[14] = row[14] || ''; return; } // leave col O as-is if no email
    const latest = latestByEmail[emailKey];
    const ts = row[8];
    const tsVal = ts instanceof Date ? ts.getTime() : Number(ts);
    if (latest && i !== latest.rowIdx && !isNaN(tsVal)) {
      row[14] = 'SUPERSEDED'; // col O
    } else {
      row[14] = ''; // clear if it's the kept one
    }
  });

  // --- Step 2: Force P=REVIEW if any of G/H/I/J is "REVIEW" ---
  data.forEach(row => {
    const anyReview = ['REVIEW'].includes(String(row[6])) // G
                   || ['REVIEW'].includes(String(row[7])) // H
                   || ['REVIEW'].includes(String(row[8])) // I
                   || ['REVIEW'].includes(String(row[9])); // J
    if (anyReview) row[15] = 'REVIEW'; // col P; otherwise leave existing formula result
  });

  // Write cols O and P back (only those two, to avoid stomping formulas elsewhere)
  const oCol = data.map(r => [r[14]]);
  const pCol = data.map(r => [r[15]]);
  raw.getRange(2, 15, numRows, 1).setValues(oCol);
  raw.getRange(2, 16, numRows, 1).setValues(pCol);

  // --- Step 3: Copy OK + non-superseded rows into "Final" as values ---
  const headers = raw.getRange(1, 1, 1, 16).getValues()[0];
  const keep = data.filter(r => String(r[15]) === 'OK' && String(r[14]) === '');

  let finalSheet = ss.getSheetByName('Final');
  if (!finalSheet) {
    finalSheet = ss.insertSheet('Final');
  } else {
    finalSheet.clearContents();
  }
  finalSheet.getRange(1, 1, 1, headers.length).setValues([headers]);
  if (keep.length) {
    finalSheet.getRange(2, 1, keep.length, headers.length).setValues(keep);
  }

  SpreadsheetApp.getActive().toast(
    `Exported ${keep.length} rows to Final. Marked ${data.filter(r => r[14]==='SUPERSEDED').length} superseded.`
  );
}
```

**A few notes:**

- It never deletes rows from `Raw`. It only writes to columns O and P and rebuilds `Final`.
- Step 2 only *forces* P to REVIEW when there's a REVIEW upstream. It won't overwrite your existing P values in other cases, so your formula in P stays accurate on re-runs. If you'd rather it clear the P formula entirely, let me know.
- SUPERSEDED is set only among rows that have an email. Rows with no email are left alone in column O (duplicate detection for those needs the name+time flag in column N).
- The first run will ask for permission to access the spreadsheet. That's normal.
- If you later add more rows to `Raw`, just run `cleanAndExport` again.

One caveat: because the script writes values into column P where upstream is REVIEW, it will replace the formula in those specific cells with the text "REVIEW". The formula still works in the other cells. If you want the P column to stay purely formula-driven, delete the Step 2 block — your formula from before already handles that case.

```javascript
function cleanAndExport() {
  const TIME_WINDOW_MIN = 10; // minutes for name+time duplicate matching

  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const raw = ss.getSheetByName('Raw');
  if (!raw) throw new Error('Sheet "Raw" not found.');

  const lastRow = raw.getLastRow();
  const lastCol = raw.getLastColumn();
  if (lastRow < 2 || lastCol < 16) return;

  // Column map (1-based):
  // 1=A Timestamp, 2=B Name, 3=C Email, 4=D JoinedBefore, 5=E Phone,
  // 6=F PreferredPark, 7=G YN_clean, 8=H Phone_clean, 9=I TS_clean,
  // 10=J Park_clean, 11=K emailKey, 12=L nameKey, 13=M DUP-email,
  // 14=N DUP-name-time, 15=O Superseded, 16=P Review
  const COL = {
    TS_CLEAN: 9, EMAIL_KEY: 11, NAME_KEY: 12,
    SUPERSEDED: 15, REVIEW: 16,
    REVIEW_SOURCES: [7, 8, 9, 10], // G,H,I,J
  };

  const numRows = lastRow - 1;
  const headers = raw.getRange(1, 1, 1, lastCol).getValues()[0];
  const data = raw.getRange(2, 1, numRows, lastCol).getValues();

  // Helper: timestamp as a number (ms), or NaN if unusable
  const tsNum = v => {
    if (v instanceof Date) return v.getTime();
    if (typeof v === 'number' && !isNaN(v)) {
      // Sheets serial date -> ms (days since 1899-12-30)
      return Math.round((v - 25569) * 86400 * 1000);
    }
    return NaN;
  };

  const windowMs = TIME_WINDOW_MIN * 60 * 1000;

  // --- Step 1a: SUPERSEDED by email (keep most recent) ---
  const latestByEmail = {}; // emailKey -> { ts, rowIdx }
  data.forEach((row, i) => {
    const key = String(row[COL.EMAIL_KEY - 1] || '').trim();
    const t = tsNum(row[COL.TS_CLEAN - 1]);
    if (!key || isNaN(t)) return;
    if (!latestByEmail[key] || t > latestByEmail[key].ts) {
      latestByEmail[key] = { ts: t, rowIdx: i };
    }
  });

  // Initialize superseded flags from the current sheet values
  const supersededOut = data.map(r => [r[COL.SUPERSEDED - 1]]);

  data.forEach((row, i) => {
    const key = String(row[COL.EMAIL_KEY - 1] || '').trim();
    const t = tsNum(row[COL.TS_CLEAN - 1]);
    if (!key || isNaN(t)) return;
    const latest = latestByEmail[key];
    supersededOut[i][0] = (latest && i !== latest.rowIdx) ? 'SUPERSEDED' : '';
  });

  // --- Step 1b: SUPERSEDED by nameKey + time window (only for rows with no email) ---
  // Group rows without email by nameKey, pick the latest-in-cluster as the keeper.
  const noEmailByName = {}; // nameKey -> [{ts, rowIdx}, ...]
  data.forEach((row, i) => {
    const email = String(row[COL.EMAIL_KEY - 1] || '').trim();
    if (email) return;
    const name = String(row[COL.NAME_KEY - 1] || '').trim();
    const t = tsNum(row[COL.TS_CLEAN - 1]);
    if (!name || isNaN(t)) return;
    (noEmailByName[name] = noEmailByName[name] || []).push({ ts: t, rowIdx: i });
  });

  Object.values(noEmailByName).forEach(entries => {
    if (entries.length < 2) return;
    // Sort by timestamp ascending
    entries.sort((a, b) => a.ts - b.ts);
    // Greedy cluster: for each entry, find all later entries within window; keep the latest in that cluster.
    const used = new Set();
    for (let a = 0; a < entries.length; a++) {
      if (used.has(a)) continue;
      const cluster = [entries[a]];
      for (let b = a + 1; b < entries.length; b++) {
        if (used.has(b)) continue;
        if (entries[b].ts - cluster[cluster.length - 1].ts <= windowMs) {
          cluster.push(entries[b]);
        }
      }
      if (cluster.length > 1) {
        const keeperRow = cluster[cluster.length - 1].rowIdx;
        cluster.forEach(e => {
          used.add(entries.indexOf(e));
          if (e.rowIdx !== keeperRow) supersededOut[e.rowIdx][0] = 'SUPERSEDED';
        });
      } else {
        used.add(a);
      }
    }
  });

  // Write column O (SUPERSEDED)
  raw.getRange(2, COL.SUPERSEDED, numRows, 1).setValues(supersededOut);

  // --- Step 2: Fill P with "REVIEW" ONLY where P is currently blank
  //            AND one of G/H/I/J is "REVIEW". Leaves existing formulas/values alone. ---
  const pRange = raw.getRange(2, COL.REVIEW, numRows, 1);
  const pValues = pRange.getValues(); // current displayed values
  const pFormulas = pRange.getFormulas();

  const pOut = pValues.map((cell, i) => {
    const current = cell[0];
    const hasFormula = pFormulas[i][0] !== '';
    if (hasFormula || (current !== '' && current !== null)) {
      return [{ formula: pFormulas[i][0], value: current, keep: true }];
    }
    const anyReview = COL.REVIEW_SOURCES.some(c => String(data[i][c - 1]) === 'REVIEW');
    return [{ value: anyReview ? 'REVIEW' : '', keep: false }];
  });

  // Only write to cells where keep=false (i.e., P was blank and no formula)
  pOut.forEach((cell, i) => {
    if (!cell[0].keep) {
      raw.getRange(i + 2, COL.REVIEW).setValue(cell[0].value);
    }
  });

  // --- Step 3: Rebuild "Final" with OK + non-superseded rows, values only ---
  // Re-read P and O after writes so Final reflects the current state.
  const finalData = raw.getRange(2, 1, numRows, lastCol).getValues();
  const keep = finalData.filter(r =>
    String(r[COL.REVIEW - 1]) === 'OK' && String(r[COL.SUPERSEDED - 1]) === ''
  );

  let finalSheet = ss.getSheetByName('Final');
  if (!finalSheet) {
    finalSheet = ss.insertSheet('Final');
  } else {
    finalSheet.clearContents();
  }
  finalSheet.getRange(1, 1, 1, lastCol).setValues([headers]);
  if (keep.length) {
    finalSheet.getRange(2, 1, keep.length, lastCol).setValues(keep);
  }

  const supersededCount = supersededOut.filter(r => r[0] === 'SUPERSEDED').length;
  SpreadsheetApp.getActive().toast(
    `Final: ${keep.length} rows. Superseded: ${supersededCount}. Window: ${TIME_WINDOW_MIN} min.`
  );
}
```

**What changed vs. the previous version:**

- **Column count** comes from `raw.getLastColumn()`, and `Final` is written with that same width. The script still requires at least 16 columns (through P) to work.
- **P column formulas are preserved.** The script reads both values and formulas from P. If a cell has a formula or a non-blank value, it's left alone. REVIEW is only written where P is truly empty and one of G/H/I/J is REVIEW.
- **Email-based SUPERSEDED** works as before: the row with the latest valid timestamp per email wins.
- **Name+time SUPERSEDED** runs only on rows with no email. It groups by `nameKey`, sorts by timestamp, and clusters entries that fall within `TIME_WINDOW_MIN` minutes of the previous one in the cluster. The latest row in each cluster is kept; the rest get SUPERSEDED. Change `TIME_WINDOW_MIN` at the top to adjust.
- **No deletions.** Only columns O and (blank) P cells in `Raw` are written; `Final` is overwritten with values only.

**One edge case to be aware of:** the name+time clustering is greedy — it chains entries that are each within the window of the previous one, which can create a longer-than-window chain if submissions are spaced out. For a 10-minute window and a human filling out a form twice, this is almost always what you want. If you'd rather require every row in a cluster to be within the window of the keeper (not the previous row), let me know and I'll swap in that version.

