**What changed:**

- **Batch writes for P.** The loop that called `setValue` per cell is gone. The script reads values and formulas once, builds one array, and writes it back with a single `setValues` + `setFormulas` pair. Cells that already had a formula or a value are written back unchanged, so nothing is clobbered.
- **No bail on narrow sheets.** `lastCol` is `max(sheetLastCol, 16)`. Reads from the sheet use the actual width, then each row is padded with empty strings out to 16 so the column-index logic (G–P) always works. If G:P are empty in your raw export, the script will leave them empty — it only writes to O and to blank P cells, as before.
- Everything else (window constant, name+time clustering, formula preservation, no deletions, Final overwrite) is unchanged.

**Caveat:** if the sheet actually has fewer than 16 columns of data, the `Final` sheet will be written 16 columns wide, with empty cells where G:P would be. That matches your current layout but is worth noting if you later wire `Final` into something downstream.

